From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:12:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Read the key of an object store's record once

A read of an object store's records with their keys, getAllRecords()
and the steps of object store cursors, selected each record's key twice,
as its key and as its primary key, which are the same for a store. On
RDB every column of every row costs a fetch through the cursor API: for
50,000 records on the DAYU200 the second key column took about 0.4 s of
the 2.85 s that the backend spent on getAllRecords(). The read now
selects the key once and the record takes it as its primary key as well.

Validation: `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits` (host SQLite): 141 passed, 1 skipped, with the store sources of test_cursor_steps_find_what_the_spec_finds (records and keys only) and test_get_all_retrieves_what_a_cursor_visits. Host WPT tests/wpt/tests/IndexedDB, 8 processes: SpiderMonkey 4,465, QuickJS 4,465 (previous commit 4,465 / 4,463), differences only known flips (SM idbversionchangeevent.any.sharedworker and idbfactory-origin-isolation swapped, QuickJS idbcursor-continuePrimaryKey-exception-order.any.sharedworker, idbfactory-origin-isolation and the lone-surrogate subtest of idbindex-rename.any.sharedworker); /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ and the interface lists 204 of 204 on SM, QuickJS as expected. DAYU200 (QuickJS + RDB, 2 processes): WPT IndexedDB/ 4,441 (previous commit 4,446), the differences in idb-partitioned-coverage, which times out as a whole there with a varying set of subtests, idbversionchangeevent.any.worker and idbobjectstore-rename-store.any.sharedworker, known flips; /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 202 of 202; `./mach test-unit --ohos -p servo-storage` RDB only 142 passed / 3 skipped, SQLite and RDB 253 / 4; the 50,000-record probe's getAllRecords() of a store took 4.65 s (previous commit 5.15 and 5.06 s), an index's 8.1 s as before; interleaved-cursors-small and idbcursor_iterating within run-to-run noise. `./mach fmt`, `./mach check --ohos -- -p servo-storage --all-targets` with SQLite, RDB and both, clippy and test-tidy as for the previous commit.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; measured the backend time of large reads on the board with a temporary timing build, changed the selected columns, reran the host and board checks)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 .../storage/indexeddb/backend/queries.rs      | 33 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/storage/indexeddb/backend/queries.rs b/components/storage/indexeddb/backend/queries.rs
index 25c297d6e1a..b75b828b77f 100644
--- a/components/storage/indexeddb/backend/queries.rs
+++ b/components/storage/indexeddb/backend/queries.rs
@@ -500,7 +500,8 @@ pub(crate) enum RecordSource<'a> {
     Index(StoreIndex),
 }
 
-/// What a read selects of each record, in this order.
+/// What a read selects of each record, in this order. A store's record has its key once, as it is
+/// also the primary key: see [`record_of_row`].
 #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]
 pub(crate) enum RecordColumns {
     /// The primary key: the key of a store's record, the value of an index's record.
@@ -551,10 +552,13 @@ impl RecordSource<'_> {
                 "o.data",
             ),
         };
+        let store = matches!(self, Self::ObjectStore(_));
         let selected = match columns {
             RecordColumns::PrimaryKey => primary_key.to_owned(),
             RecordColumns::Value => format!("{primary_key}, {value}"),
+            RecordColumns::Record if store => format!("{key}, {value}"),
             RecordColumns::Record => format!("{key}, {primary_key}, {value}"),
+            RecordColumns::Keys if store => key.to_owned(),
             RecordColumns::Keys => format!("{key}, {primary_key}"),
         };
         (format!("{from}{}", condition.on(key)), selected)
@@ -685,11 +689,26 @@ pub(crate) fn get_key<X: SqlExecutor>(
     .pop())
 }
 
-fn record_of_row(row: &dyn SqlRow, with_value: bool) -> Result<IndexedDBRecord, SqlError> {
+/// The record of `source` in a row of [`RecordColumns::Record`], or of [`RecordColumns::Keys`]
+/// without `with_value`.
+fn record_of_row(
+    source: RecordSource,
+    row: &dyn SqlRow,
+    with_value: bool,
+) -> Result<IndexedDBRecord, SqlError> {
+    let key = decode_key(&row.blob(0)?)?;
+    let (primary_key, value_column) = match source {
+        RecordSource::ObjectStore(_) => (key.clone(), 1),
+        RecordSource::Index(_) => (decode_key(&row.blob(1)?)?, 2),
+    };
     Ok(IndexedDBRecord {
-        key: decode_key(&row.blob(0)?)?,
-        primary_key: decode_key(&row.blob(1)?)?,
-        value: if with_value { Some(row.blob(2)?) } else { None },
+        key,
+        primary_key,
+        value: if with_value {
+            Some(row.blob(value_column)?)
+        } else {
+            None
+        },
     })
 }
 
@@ -811,7 +830,7 @@ pub(crate) fn get_all_records<X: SqlExecutor>(
         range,
         direction,
         count,
-        |row| record_of_row(row, true),
+        |row| record_of_row(source, row, true),
     )
 }
 
@@ -1002,7 +1021,7 @@ pub(crate) fn cursor_records<X: SqlExecutor>(
         reverse,
         Some(records),
         offset,
-        |row| record_of_row(row, !key_only),
+        |row| record_of_row(source, row, !key_only),
     )
 }
 
